E22  FURTHER INTRINSICALLY DISCRETE (R2) COHORTS
     Four cohorts is thin support for a claim about cohort-specific
     crossovers, so this looks for more and FITS them rather than
     listing what might be possible.
====================================================================================================
  DRSA archive:
    CLINIC     available   T=50    discrete=True
    MUSIC      available   T=237   discrete=True
    The archive ships exactly these two splits; there is no third.

  SPARCS: every APR-DRG is a distinct patient population measured on the
  same whole-day scale, so each viable code is a NEW R2 cohort rather
  than a re-slice of an old one.  Scanning for the largest.
    twelve largest APR-DRGs: 640(207,764), 560(151,659), 540(79,702), 720(66,790), 194(53,966), 139(49,801), 140(47,397), 383(41,720), 201(38,881), 860(35,865), 750(34,968), 302(34,233)

  cohort                 n    T   modal        D_T     NB SE   verdict
  sparcs/drg640     207764   30  0.5858   +0.09995   0.00123   discrete wins
  sparcs/drg560     151659   30  0.6015   +0.13645   0.00157   discrete wins
  sparcs/drg540      79702   30  0.4617   +0.08001   0.00225   discrete wins
  sparcs/drg720      66790   30  0.0995   +0.00308   0.00031   discrete wins

